# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so everything not excluded here is shipped to
# the daemon and lands in an intermediate layer. Two reasons that matters:
# .envrc.local holds the ed25519 key that grants publish rights over
# io.noetive/*, and installer/node_modules is 26 MB the Go build never reads.

.git
.github
.githooks

# Credentials. The final image is distroless and copies only the binary, so
# nothing here reaches a published layer — but the build context and the local
# layer cache are not nothing.
#
# `**/` on every one of these: docker matches with filepath.Match, where `*`
# does not cross a `/`, so a bare `*.pem` covers the root and nothing else. The
# same patterns in .gitignore do match at any depth, which makes the two files
# look equivalent when they are not.
**/.env
**/.envrc
**/.envrc.local
**/.envrc.*.local
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# The npm wrapper is a separate artifact with a separate pipeline; the image
# runs the Go binary directly.
installer/
scripts/
packaging/
docs/
skills/
tools/

# Build output, from here or from a previous run.
dist/
bin/
tmp/
**/*.test
**/*.out
.mutation-salvage.json

# Editor and agent state.
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

*.md
!README.md
